{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjrcxsDcEZTPajCVMMmf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011P6e8JYWiTqXfwnnja9AoH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat >> notes/issues.md <<'E'\n14. island visuals: the low side of the tilted island sat under the sea (screenshot pass); lifted the island group\n15. ui: the Who's Here mats wrapped and spilled outside the safe margin; page switchers counted as a seventh choice (ui audit)\n16. touch-only state was not cleared when a key was pressed during attract (ui test)\n17. hub harness: a flaky \"ghost: every copy sends its player\" failure in the host-leaves run under heavy machine load; passed on rerun\nE\ncat > ../exit-interview.json <<'E'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-05 05:22:01\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (built without Still Water, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace and Island Loop, which the plan's cut order allows; ten classes plus the Check-In remain)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Physics-balance party sports with a daily-ritual progression\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third person: framed stage cameras per event, orbitable chase camera on the island\",\n    \"tech\": \"Three.js R180 (0.180.0, WebGPU backend with WebGL2 fallback, TSL toon and ink post), Rapier 0.19.3 (@dimforge/rapier3d-compat), Web Audio, Gamepad API, esbuild 0.28.2, Playwright 1.63.0, Fredoka 5.3.0 (@fontsource/fredoka)\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"Cel-shaded ink filter over a wooden-toy resort, all models made in code on Three.js's own materials\",\n    \"animation\": \"Three.js AnimationMixer clips on jointed rigs, procedural lean from the physics, Rapier ragdolls\",\n    \"audio\": \"Code-synthesised city-pop and bossa at 10% by default, synthesised sound effects, Animalese and Simlish-style gibberish voices; no audio files\",\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub Session Protocol v1 in ghost mode for 1-4 devices, plus 1-4 players on one screen (Group Class)\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless scripts that play the game and check its state, including a scripted playthrough of the whole five-day programme through the real menus with bots and a stubbed gamepad; one command (node tools/test.mjs full) that prints only failures and a one-line count; groups unit, events, balance, flow, input, audio, ui and hub (the AI Hub harness at 1, 2 and 4 players, bad network and host leaving); screenshots only for the art pass; no subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit\",\n    \"research\": \"The AI Hub session protocol page and client; the supplied PLAN.md. No other research\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"17 issues were caught and logged as they happened (notes/issues.md): bot and balance runs, the whole-game playthrough, the unit greps, the forced-fall test, the UI audit and the screenshot pass.\",\n    \"7 were critical or game breaking: NaN lean in every event, dives that never launched, a Rapier panic when a world had no ground, a bot that did not exist when switched on mid-event, a morning script that died on a missing question list, a jar screen whose Skip looped forever, and check-in tests ending each other early.\",\n    \"The scripted playthrough of all five days through the real menus with bots: it found the jar hang, the dead morning script and the check-in timer bug that no single-event test could see.\",\n    \"The wall-clock attract run: it needs about twelve real seconds and found nothing that the advance()-driven attract check had not already shown.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"toonOutlinePass plus a short TSL post pass gave the whole ink look with no extra assets, and the same code ran on WebGPU and the WebGL2 fallback. Rapier's ball joints and a torque-limited controller made falling feel like a toy.\",\n    \"Yes. Rapier panicked with a bare 'unreachable' when an event world had no ground collider after a ragdoll recovered, and the fix was a one-line ground. I also guessed wrong about a pipe hiding test output and a stray heredoc that hung a shell.\",\n    \"The balance core (a torque-limited controller on a ball joint), the ragdoll built from the rig's joints, the input layer with latched taps, the DOM menu system and every synthesised sound.\",\n    \"Knowing what was really happening: a Rapier panic gives no message and kills physics for the page, and headless WebGPU only draws with the right flags.\",\n    \"None.\",\n    \"Make Rapier's panics catchable errors that say which handle or removal caused them.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan: exact numbers, traps already found, a ready recipe for the ink look and a hub contract that could be tested with the real harness.\",\n    \"How large the plan was for one medium-effort run: thirteen events plus a full shell is a lot, and it was not clear which parts could be cut first beyond the cut order.\",\n    \"Fitting every system (programme, hub session, attract, dev mode, group class, touch-only, audio) into one build and still testing the whole game; I cut four events to finish.\",\n    \"Ship the plan's prototype code as a starting repository, and split the build into stages so each stage can be tested before the next.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"Wiggle Fit\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Straighten the crooked island, one class at a time\",\n    \"description\": \"A wooden-toy wellness retreat on a crooked island, where you hold poses, stack stones and catch fruit with real balance physics, and straighten the whole island one class at a time.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"series\": \"\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"Lean: stick, WASD or mouse. Feet: L2 R2, Q E or clicks. Flail: Square or F\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"comedy\", \"third-person\", \"versus\", \"arcade\"]\n  }\n}\nE\nnode -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('../exit-interview.json','utf8')); console.log('json ok')\"; node tools/build.mjs | tail -1; tools/bg.sh full node tools/test.mjs full; echo started"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2022,"cache_read_input_tokens":480929,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2022},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc2a51a5-f08a-42e7-afc4-8d441845bc15","uuid":"33c646e6-be69-42b1-a38d-ccb7495c17ff","timestamp":"2026-11-05T13:25:50.417Z","request_id":"req_011CgjrcxKjK9SHZBU6tYiUY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011P6e8JYWiTqXfwnnja9AoH":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-052201__x29b4d9/work/WiggleFit-WiiFit-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-052201 && cat >> notes/issues.md <<'E'\n14. island visuals: the low side of the tilted island sat under the sea (screenshot pass); lifted the island group\n15. ui: the Who's Here mats wrapped and spilled outside the safe margin; page switchers counted as a seventh choice (ui audit)\n16. touch-only state was not cleared when a key was pressed during attract (ui test)\n17. hub harness: a flaky \"ghost: every copy sends its player\" failure in the host-leaves run under heavy machine load; passed on rerun\nE\ncat > ../exit-interview.json <<'E'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-05 05:22:01\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md (built without Still Water, Plank & Perch, Tug of Peace and Island Loop, which the plan's cut order allows; ten classes plus the Check-In remain)\",\n    \"genre\": \"Physics-balance party